  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Malians carry a Muslim first name in a local form (Seydou for Saïdou, Bakary for Abu Bakr, Fousseyni for Hussein) and a family name (jamu) passed down from the father. The jamu places a family: Traoré, Diarra and Coulibaly are Bambara; Keïta and Konaté are Malinke; Diallo and Sidibé are Fulani; Cissé and Sylla are Soninke. Each jamu has its own greeting and joking partners (senankuya), so a Traoré and a Diarra may tease each other warmly when they meet. Girls are often named after a grandmother, and nicknames like Madou, Nana or Mah are common.",
